{title: Michael, Row the Boat Ashore}
{artist: Traditional spiritual}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Closing}
{style: Spiritual}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Michael, row the boat a[C]shore, halle[G]lujah
[G]Michael, row the boat a[C]shore, halle[G]lujah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Sister, help to trim the [C]sail, halle[G]lujah
[G]Sister, help to trim the [C]sail, halle[G]lujah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Jordan River is chilly and [C]cold, halle[G]lujah
[G]Chills the body but not the [C]soul, halle[G]lujah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Jordan River is deep and [C]wide, halle[G]lujah
[G]Meet my mother on the other [C]side, halle[G]lujah
{end_of_verse}
